  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Let $a=\u27e82,-1,-2\u27e9$ and $b=\u27e8x,-4,0\u27e9.$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$",
  "worked_solution": "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na\u22a5b\\,\u27f9\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =2\\cdot x+(-1)\\cdot (-4)+(-2)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =2x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 2x+4 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =-4 \\\\ x & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
